{"processInformation": {"dataSetInformation": {"UUID": "b38b2ec7-fdef-4260-a19b-97e81b8a5572", "name": {"baseName": [{"value": "Tyvek® Monolayer 60 (1060B, 1560B, 2460B)", "lang": "en"}], "functionalUnitFlowProperties": [{"lang": "en"}]}, "classificationInformation": {"classification": [{"class": [{"value": "Kunststoffe", "level": 0, "classId": "6"}, {"value": "Folien und Vliese", "level": 1, "classId": "6.6"}, {"value": "Folien zur Abdichtung", "level": 2, "classId": "6.6.03"}], "name": "OEKOBAU.DAT"}, {"class": [{"value": "02 Building products", "level": 0}, {"value": "Membranes, including Liquid applied and kits", "level": 1}, {"value": "False ceiling and underlay sheeting", "level": 2}], "name": "IBUCategories"}]}, "generalComment": [{"value": "DuPont™ Tyvek® is a nonwoven material made of HDPE, which is diffusion open but watertight. It is used as a roof and wall underlay.", "lang": "en"}]}, "quantitativeReference": {"referenceToReferenceFlow": [0]}, "time": {"referenceYear": 2021, "dataSetValidUntil": 2026, "other": {"anies": [{"name": "publicationDateOfEPD", "value": 1638230400000}]}}, "geography": {"locationOfOperationSupplyOrProduction": {"location": "LU"}}, "technology": {"technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses": [{"value": "The production process follows different steps. First, the monolayer is produced at DuPont in Luxembourg-Contern from the spinning and bonding of high-density polyethylene (HDPE). The rolls are then put on pallets using cardboard, stretch film and cores as packaging materials. The HDPE waste is pelletized with water and is either internally recycled or externally sold depending on the quality. The various machines and the daily functioning of the site lead to the consumption of water, steam, compressed air, electricity, diesel oil and natural gas. The printing and converting to customers’ dimensions specifications is done in another plant in Germany. The production line (printing, cutting and packaging) consumes colour paste, water, electricity, diesel oil, natural gas, forklift gas and packaging materials (pallets, carton cores, stretch film and carton edge protection). The plant generates Tyvek® and hazardous chemicals (colours) waste which are incinerated, as well as PE film waste which is recycled externally. \nTechnical data: \nThe following chapter comprises technical data for the characteristics listed in the Declaration of Performance according to the harmonized technical specifications EN 13859-1 and EN 13859-2. \nDeclared unit: \nThis declaration applies to 1 m2 of DuPont™ Tyvek® 1060B, 1560B and 2460B membranes, with a declared unit weight of 58 g/m2. \nThe product 1060B uses a different bonder for processing, while the products 1560B and 2460B only differ from the printed pattern.", "lang": "en"}], "technologicalApplicability": [{"value": "Tyvek® underlays are used in roofs and walls. They constitute the second water-shedding layer and at the same time protect the insulation from trapped moisture, wind penetration, dust and insects. Insulation installed below Tyvek® is kept dry and performs as designed.", "lang": "en"}]}}, "modellingAndValidation": {"LCIMethodAndAllocation": {"typeOfDataSet": "EPD", "referenceToLCAMethodDetails": [{"shortDescription": [{"value": "False ceiling and underlay sheeting.pdf", "lang": "en"}], "type": "source data set", "refObjectId": "e13901ad-9118-420c-ac6d-3ab14f51545a"}], "other": {"anies": [{"name": "subType", "value": "specific dataset"}]}}, "dataSourcesTreatmentAndRepresentativeness": {"referenceToDataSource": [{"shortDescription": [{"value": "GaBi Database (all versions)", "lang": "en"}], "type": "source data set", "refObjectId": "28d74cc0-db8b-4d7e-bc44-5f6d56ce0c4a"}, {"shortDescription": [{"value": "GaBi Database Edition 2021, CUP 2021.02", "lang": "en"}], "type": "source data set", "refObjectId": "90321ffe-9ebb-4946-886c-338efe6fbf26"}], "useAdviceForDataSet": [{"value": "Scope: \nThis document applies to DuPont™ Tyvek® 1060B, 1560B and 2460B monolayer high density polyethylene (HDPE) membranes manufactured by DuPont in L-2984 Contern and printed in Germany, with a declared unit weight of 58 g/m2. The LCA data were compiled using production data from the year 2019 by DuPont Luxembourg s.à r.l. The declaration holder is responsible for the underlying data and its verification. \nSystem boundary: \nType of EPD: Cradle-to-gate (with options)\n\nThe system boundaries of the EPD follow the modular construction system as described by EN 15804. The LCA takes into account the following modules: \n\nA1-A3: Manufacturing of pre-products, packaging, ancillary materials, transport to the factory, production including energy supply and waste handling\nA4: Transport to the construction site\nA5: Installation into the building (disposal of packaging)\nC4: Waste disposal (incineration)\n\nD: Potential for reuse, recovery and/or recycling (benefits for incineration and recovery of packaging materials from module A5 and envelopes incineration from module C4).", "lang": "en"}], "other": {"anies": [{"name": "referenceToOriginalEPD", "value": {"shortDescription": {"value": "Tyvek® Monolayer 60 (1060B, 1560B, 2460B).pdf", "defaultValue": "Tyvek® Monolayer 60 (1060B, 1560B, 2460B).pdf", "lstrings": [{"lang": "en", "value": "Tyvek® Monolayer 60 (1060B, 1560B, 2460B).pdf"}]}, "type": "source data set", "uuid": {"uuid": "88b9ecc5-fa04-401b-b6a7-c71e9f6c1395"}, "refObjectId": "88b9ecc5-fa04-401b-b6a7-c71e9f6c1395", "resourceURLs": ["https://oekobaudat.de/OEKOBAU.DAT/resource/sources/88b9ecc5-fa04-401b-b6a7-c71e9f6c1395/Tyvek_Monolayer_60_1060B_1560B_2460B__24124.pdf?version=00.02.000"]}}]}}, "validation": {"review": [{"referenceToNameOfReviewerAndInstitution": [{"shortDescription": [{"value": "Institut Bauen und Umwelt e. V.", "lang": "en"}], "type": "contact data set", "refObjectId": "d111dbec-b024-4be5-86c5-752d6eb2cf95", "uri": "../contacts/d111dbec-b024-4be5-86c5-752d6eb2cf95.xml"}], "type": "Accredited third party review"}]},